A section-aware theme is a good instinct, and it maps directly onto Diátaxis — each quadrant has a different reading mode, so a different treatment is communicating something, not decorating. The trick is keeping it subtle: an accent, a label, a spacing rhythm. Not a different site per section.

The design
Section	Accent	Label	Treatment
start	green	Tutorial	generous spacing, step-timeline on h2s, reading progress bar
guides	silver	Guide	compact, task-shaped h2s
concepts	steel blue	Concept	prose measure, larger type, wider leading
reference	muted	Reference	dense, tight tables, wider grid
background	amber	Background	prose treatment plus a persistent "not about Ingot" mark
contributing	silver	Contributing	neutral
decisions	muted	Decision record	monospace metadata, archival feel

Section comes from the URL automatically, with a frontmatter override (section: tutorial) for pages that don't live where they belong.

