markdown
# Units and libraries

Ingot compiles every unit — every library, every block — into its own
VCS library, once, and shares that compiled result with everything that
depends on it. This page explains what that means, why it's the default,
and what it costs.

## What a unit is

A unit is a directory with an `ingot.toml`. That's the whole definition.
Libraries declare `[library]`; blocks declare `[block]`. The manifest
names the unit, and the name is what other units use to depend on it.

```mermaid
graph LR
  ing[ing<br/><small>lib/ing</small>] --> dma[dma<br/><small>blocks/dma</small>]
  ing --> uart[uart<br/><small>blocks/uart</small>]
  ingv[ingv<br/><small>lib/ingv</small>] --> dma
  ingv --> uart
  dma --> top[top<br/><small>blocks/top</small>]
  uart --> top
```

Nothing about the directory path matters to resolution. `lib/` and
`blocks/` exist to tell humans which things are meant to outlive the
project, not to tell Ingot anything.

## What "its own library" means

VCS's three-step flow analyzes sources into a *compiled library* — a
directory of parsed, type-checked design units — and elaborates from
there. The default is one library for everything.

Ingot gives each unit its own:

```
build/
├── ing/an/base/AN.DB
├── ingv/an/base/AN.DB
├── dma/an/base/AN.DB
└── top/
    ├── an/base/AN.DB
    └── fast/synopsys_sim.setup      ← maps all five by name
```

When `top` is elaborated, VCS finds `dma`'s modules in `dma`'s library,
`ing`'s in `ing`'s, and so on, through a generated setup file. Nothing
gets re-analyzed for `top`'s benefit.

> A block is a library when another block depends on it. The compiled
> output is the same directory whether you're running `dma`'s testbench or
> building `top` against it.

## Why this is the default

Three reasons, in order of how much they matter.

**Analysis is shared.** Without per-unit libraries, building `top`
re-analyzes every source in the design. With them, `ing` was analyzed
once — when the first block needed it — and every block since has reused
that work. On a design where the library carries UVM and vendor VIP, that
is the difference between seconds and minutes per block.

**Only what changed re-analyzes.** Each library has a stamp recording
what went into it. Edit `dma_engine.sv` and `dma` re-analyzes; `ing`,
`ingv`, and `uart` don't. Then `-Mupdate` recompiles only the affected
modules at elaboration. The incremental story is end to end.

**Partition compile is a flag flip.** VCS's `-partcomp` partitions along
library boundaries. With per-unit libraries already in place, enabling it
later is a profile change, not a restructure.

## What it costs

**Disk.** Each unit has an analysis directory, and each block has one
elaboration directory per profile. `ingot clean --profile debug` exists
for when that adds up.

**A setup file you never touch.** `synopsys_sim.setup` is generated into
every working directory. You can read it — `ingot manifest show` prints
the mapping — but you don't write it.

**Cross-library imports have to work.** `import dma_pkg::*` inside `top`'s
environment resolves through the setup file into `dma`'s library. That's
standard three-step methodology, but it's a moving part, and it's the
thing worth verifying first when a new block can't see a dependency's
package.

## Where defines fit

A define changes what the analyzer sees, so it changes the analysis.
Blocks whose effective defines differ get separate analyses of the same
library:

```
build/ing/an/base/          ← every block with no defines
build/ing/an/9f2a11c3e0b4/  ← blocks that set +define+FIFO_DEPTH=16
```

Most blocks have no defines and share `base`. The keyed directories exist
so that the ones that do can't corrupt everyone else's.

## Related

- [Profiles](profiles.md) — the same idea applied to elaboration
- [Incremental compilation](incremental-compilation.md) — exactly what
  gets skipped and why
- [Compiled libraries](../background/compiled-libraries.md) — the VCS
  background if this is new
docs/reference/manifest.md
markdown
# Manifest

Every unit is defined by an `ingot.toml` at its root. This page lists
every section and field. Unknown keys are errors, not warnings.

## Unit manifests

A unit manifest carries exactly one of `[block]` or `[library]`.

### `[block]`

A design under test. Has a testbench; may have tests.

`name`
:   Unique across every unit in the project. Becomes the compiled library
    name. **Required.**

`top`
:   Module elaboration starts from. The testbench top, not the DUT.
    Required for `ingot build`.

`dut`
:   Instance name of the design under `top`. Used to scope coverage.
    Default `"dut"`.

### `[library]`

A collection of components. Depended on, never run directly.

`name`
:   Unique across every unit. Becomes the compiled library name.
    **Required.**

!!! note "Libraries cannot have `[tests]`"

    Libraries are exercised by unit tests, not testbenches. If a unit has
    a DUT and needs a UVM environment to verify, it is a block — declare
    it as one, wherever it lives.

### `[dependencies]`

```toml
[dependencies]
ing  = "*"
ingv = "*"
```

Keys are unit names, resolved by scanning `lib/` and `blocks/` for a
manifest with a matching `name`. Values are version constraints;
currently only `"*"` is meaningful. Dependencies resolve transitively and
cycles are errors.

### `[sources]`

All fields optional. Defaults discover sources by convention.

| Field | Type | Default | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|
| `include` | list | see below | Glob patterns replacing the defaults |
| `exclude` | list | `[]` | Glob patterns removed from the result |
| `order` | list | `[]` | Path suffixes forced to the front, for VHDL |
| `incdirs` | list | `[]` | Extra include directories, relative to the unit |
| `compile` | list | `[]` | Header files that must be compiled directly |
| `library` | string | `"work"` | VHDL library name |

Default `include` patterns:

```
design/**/*.{sv,svh,v,vh,vhd,vhdl}
verif/**/*.{sv,svh}
src/**/*.{sv,svh}
*.{sv,svh,v,vh,vhd,vhdl}
```

Blocks use `design/` and `verif/`. Libraries put sources at their root
or under `src/`. Anything else needs `include`.

**Headers.** Files ending `.svh` or `.vh` are discovered, contribute their
directory to the include path, and are *not* passed to the compiler —
they are included by other files. List a header under `compile` if it
must be compiled directly. `ingot manifest show` names every excluded
header.

**Ordering.** VHDL sources are ordered automatically by scanning
`use work.X` and `entity work.X` references. `order` overrides that for
files the scanner gets wrong. SystemVerilog needs no ordering within a
single analysis.

### `[defines]`

```toml
[defines]
SIMULATION = ""
FIFO_DEPTH = "16"
```

Emitted as `+define+KEY=VALUE`, or `+define+KEY` when the value is empty.
Merged across the dependency chain — a block's defines override its
dependencies'. Any define changes the analysis key, so blocks with
different defines get separate analyses of shared libraries.

### `[tests.<name>]`

```toml
[tests.smoke]
seeds = 1

[tests.stress]
seeds = 20
plusargs = ["+iterations=2000"]
```

`seeds`
:   How many random seeds `ingot regress` runs for this test. Default `1`.

`plusargs`
:   Passed to `simv` after the standard `+UVM_TESTNAME` and
    `+ntb_random_seed`. Default `[]`.

Blocks only. The test name becomes `+UVM_TESTNAME`; non-UVM testbenches
ignore it.

### `[profiles.<name>]`

Block-level profile overrides. Same schema as the project-level section
below. Use for something specific to one block — `-partcomp` on `top`,
say — not for redefining what `debug` means.

## Project manifest

The root `ingot.toml` is identified by carrying `[project]` or
`[gitlab]`. It is not a unit.

### `[project]`

`name`
:   Project name. Informational.

### `[gitlab]`

`url`
:   Instance URL.

`project`
:   Path with namespace, e.g. `circuitware/ingot/ingot`.

`ca_bundle`
:   Path to the corporate CA certificate. Overridden by
    `REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE`.

### `[agent]`

`name`, `email`
:   Identity used for the `Co-authored-by` trailer on AI-assisted commits.

### `[profiles.<name>]`

```toml
[profiles.gate]
description = "Gate-level with SDF timing."
inherits    = "fast"
defines     = { GATE_SIM = "" }
elab_args   = ["-sdf", "max:dut:netlist.sdf"]
```

| Field | Type | Default | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|
| `description` | string | `""` | Shown by `ingot profiles` |
| `inherits` | string | — | Parent profile; ancestors apply first |
| `elab_args` | list | `[]` | Appended to the `vcs` command |
| `defines` | table | `{}` | Profile-specific defines; forces a separate analysis |
| `coverage` | bool | `false` | Add `-cm` and generate a hierarchy file |
| `coverage_metrics` | string | `"line+cond+fsm+tgl+branch"` | The `-cm` argument |
| `coverage_scope` | string | `"dut"` | `"dut"` scopes to `top.dut`; `"all"` covers everything |

Built-in profiles `fast`, `debug`, and `coverage` may be overridden by
name. See [Profiles](profiles.md) for their definitions.

## Complete example

```toml
[block]
name = "dma"                 # (1)!
top  = "dma_tb"
dut  = "u_dma"               # (2)!

[dependencies]
ing  = "*"
ingv = "*"

[sources]
exclude = ["design/legacy/**"]
incdirs = ["verif/include"]  # (3)!

[defines]
DMA_CHANNELS = "4"

[tests.smoke]
seeds = 1

[tests.burst_wrap]
seeds = 25
plusargs = ["+max_burst=256"]

[profiles.fast]              # (4)!
inherits  = "fast"
elab_args = ["-timescale=1ns/1ps"]
```

1. Also the compiled library name — `dma` in `synopsys_sim.setup`.
2. The DUT is instantiated as `u_dma`, not `dut`, so coverage scope
   needs telling.
3. Directories containing `.svh` files are found automatically; this
   adds one that has no discovered sources of its own.
4. Overrides the built-in `fast` for this block only, adding a
   timescale.
