markdown
# The three-step flow

VCS can compile a design in one command or three. Ingot uses three, and
most of what makes it fast depends on the difference.

## One step

```bash
vcs -sverilog design.sv tb.sv -o simv
```

Parse, type-check, elaborate, generate C, compile C, link. One invocation,
one output. Simple, and every change to any file repeats all of it.

## Three steps

```bash
vlogan -sverilog design.sv tb.sv     # analyze
vcs tb_top -o simv                   # elaborate
./simv                               # run
```

**Analysis** parses and type-checks each file into a *compiled library* —
a directory of design units VCS can load later. It's per-file and fast.

**Elaboration** starts from a top module, resolves every instantiation
against the compiled libraries, flattens the hierarchy, and generates
and compiles the simulation binary. This is the expensive step, and it's
where debug access, coverage instrumentation, and optimization flags
apply.

**Run** executes the binary with plusargs — test name, seed, verbosity.

## Why the split matters

Three things become possible that aren't with one step.

**Analysis can be shared.** A library analyzed once serves every design
that instantiates it. In one-step, every design re-analyzes everything.

**Elaboration can vary without re-analysis.** Debug and non-debug
binaries come from the same compiled libraries. Flags that change the
binary don't change what was parsed.

**Runs are free.** A thousand seeds against one binary cost one
elaboration. In one-step, tools that recompile per test pay elaboration
a thousand times — and that's more common than you'd expect.

Ingot's [profiles](../concepts/profiles.md) are the second point made
into a feature. Its [per-unit libraries](../concepts/units-and-libraries.md)
are the first.

## The setup file

Three-step needs to know where compiled libraries live. That's
`synopsys_sim.setup`, read from the working directory:

```
WORK > DEFAULT
DEFAULT : /abs/build/dma/an/base/AN.DB
ing     : /abs/build/ing/an/base/AN.DB
```

Library names on the left, directories on the right. `vlogan -work ing`
writes into the `ing` entry; `vcs` reads all of them. Ingot generates
this file; you won't edit it.

## Read more

- VCS User Guide, "Three-Step Flow" — the authoritative description
- [Compiled libraries](compiled-libraries.md) — what's inside `AN.DB`
- [Incremental compilation](../concepts/incremental-compilation.md) —
  how Ingot decides what to skip
